@startuml
title Registry as a sorted linked list, with the two proof shapes
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5

rectangle "Origin node\nkey = <empty>\nnext = 0x3a1c..." as O
rectangle "Node A\nkey = 0x3a1c...\nnext = 0x7f04..." as A
rectangle "Node B\nkey = 0x7f04...\nnext = 0xff..ff" as B
rectangle "Sentinel\n0xff..ff (30 bytes)" as S #F2F2F2

O -right-> A
A -right-> B
B -right-> S

rectangle "TokenExists { node_idx }\nnode.key == 0x7f04...\nthe policy is registered" as P1 #DCE9FA
rectangle "TokenDoesNotExist { node_idx }\n0x3a1c... < 0x5b90... < 0x7f04...\nthe policy is an ordinary native asset" as P2 #DCE9FA

P1 .up.> B
P2 .up.> A

note bottom of P2
  Sorted order plus completeness
  make a covering node a proof of
  absence, so a lookup costs one
  reference input either way.
end note
@enduml
